{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_irqhkyz62rpqrrmyws3l6n35wz4mvsa5zkte4mxjajk2ajchyg2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit (`src/lib.c`, 557 lines) — a slice of the **cute_c2 / tinyc2** 2D collision library: the GJK distance algorithm plus its vector/rotation/transform math, simplex solvers, and the `gjk_cache` entry point declared in `include/lib.h`. Every C function has external linkage, so **all 31** are part of the public ABI (no namespace-renaming macros in the headers — checked).\n\n## Deliverables\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — full translation; all 31 functions `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`, `#[repr(C)]` structs (`c2v`, `c2r`, `c2x`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`, `c2Capsule`, `c2GJKCache`, `c2Proxy`, `c2sv`, `c2Simplex`) laid out identically to C — including the `c2sv a,b,c,d` members modeled as `verts: [c2sv;4]` so the C idiom `c2sv* verts = &s->a; verts[i]` maps directly.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- `gjk_cache` **never writes through its `a9`/`b9` out-params** — reproduced verbatim, along with its dead `d0`/`d1` computations that still mutate the cache.\n- The inverted cache-validation test `!(min_metric < max_metric*2 && metric < -1.0e8f)` kept as-is.\n- Ternary min/max in `c2Maxv`/`c2Minv` written as explicit comparisons (not `f32::max`) to keep C's NaN fall-through.\n- `switch` fall-through in `c2GJKSimplexMetric` (`default:` → `case 1:`) and the missing `default:` in `c2MakeProxy` (bogus type ⇒ proxy left untouched).\n- Exact check ordering in `c22`/`c23`/`c2GJK`, and the literal `FLT_MAX`/`FLT_EPSILON` constants.\n\n## Verification (independently run, not self-reported)\n1. **Symbol parity:** `nm -D` diff of C `.so` vs Rust `.so` → **31 vs 31, empty diff both directions**.\n2. **Differential harness:** a C driver `dlopen`s both libraries and exercises **all 31 exported symbols** — 400 math-helper rounds (incl. NaN/±inf/−0.0), all 4 `c2MakeProxy` type branches, 600 simplex cases seeded with **randomized garbage over the whole struct** (so any layout mismatch would surface), 1500 `c2GJK` cases across all 9 shape pairs × null/non-null transforms/outputs/iterations/cache × warm-cache reuse, and 400+ `gjk_cache` calls plus a 121-case extreme/degenerate parameter sweep. Results dumped as raw float bit patterns and raw struct bytes: **1,137,881 bytes byte-identical**.\n3. **Optimization-independence:** C rebuilt at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3` — all four **identical** to the Rust output, confirming the match isn't an artifact of one codegen setting.\n\nOne caveat worth stating: an earlier harness revision also fed `c2GJK` a hand-seeded cache whose vertex indices exceeded the proxy's vertex count. That makes the C read **uninitialized stack** (`c2Proxy pA;` is never fully initialized), so its output there is genuine UB garbage that no implementation can match bit-for-bit; Rust deterministically zero-initializes instead. This path is unreachable through the library's own API — cache indices always originate from a prior `c2GJK` call on the same shape pair, and `gjk_cache` itself only ever reuses a cache with matching shapes. Restricting the seeded indices to the valid range eliminated every diff.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles cleanly with no warnings, and nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":49653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1455,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60a1a375-3dbf-4433-892b-78f9506feedd","uuid":"8f6fa78e-a547-4a2b-bf25-2df565455249","timestamp":"2026-08-20T03:06:58.368Z"}
